%% C4 Dynamic Diagram - per-request path through the Core container.
%% Same sequence for benchmark replay and runtime middleware.
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant W as Workload<br/>(JSONL trace<br/>or live traffic)
  participant R as AdmitPerf runner
  participant S as State cache<br/>(refreshed on engine tick)
  participant P as Policy plugin<br/>(e.g. Chronos-inspired)
  participant E as Engine<br/>(vLLM / SGLang / replay)
  participant M as Metrics collector

  Note over S,E: State is pushed on the engine's own cadence,<br/>never scraped per arrival.
  E-->>S: tick: KV%, queue depth, running reqs

  W->>R: request arrives (arrival_time, tokens, SLO class)
  R->>S: read latest snapshot (no I/O)
  S-->>R: SystemState (with staleness age)
  R->>P: decide(request, state)
  P-->>R: ADMIT | DEFER(50ms) | REJECT("kv_pressure")

  alt ADMIT
    R->>E: enqueue for inference
    E-->>M: TTFT, TBT, completion
  else DEFER
    R->>R: hold until retry_after_ms OR next state tick
    R->>P: decide(request, fresher state)
  else REJECT
    R->>M: log 429 with reason
  end

  M-->>M: update goodput, admit/defer/reject counts
